Victory screenshot: http://crankgod.rocketjump.org/general/sacrifice.PNG

It's too bad I stopped playing on the tournament server after I lost a
Valk down in Moloch's sanctum. I think I'll use that dilithium star
banner anyway :)

I decided to pay more attention to spellcasting for this monk, whereas
I usually ignore it completely. I got a few useful spells here and
there, and a forgotten spell was useful for the Planes, but it still
didn't really pan out that much.

I don't remember the very early game too well, but I probably followed
my usual routine: explore the dungeons until I have some decent HP,
find minetown (which turned out to be coaligned), do sokoban (bag of
holding), then finish the mines (got the mimic level). At some point i
found some 300-bracket scrolls, which were blessed, so I read them;
genocide! L and h were out of the picture, and with my starting magic
marker (0:89) I wrote another and killed off ;.

At this point I was kind of concerned about unihorns. The only unicorn
I'd seen so far was grey, so killing it wasn't an option. Still, I
pressed on, and found the quest at DL12 (same as my XP was at the
time). No unihorn. Kept exploring, and found a !oGL, so I decided to
just fight my way to XL13 and use the potion to open up the quest.

I found a lep hall with an amulet of life saving on DL17. I lost it on
DL19 during an accident involving teleportitis, a floating eye, a
vrock, and a titanothere.

I found Medusa on DL23, and was a bit leery of going deeper, but when
the titan went down in 5 hits I decided to just go ahead. FINALLY
found a unihorn on medusa's island. M died to a looking glass and P
had levitation boots. Nearly died twice in the maze under medusa,
first to a minotaur and again to a golden naga.

The castle was mostly uneventful, except for two things. One, the wand
was at 0:3 (awesome). Two, after not getting magic resistance until I
wished for a +2 greased firerpoof cloak of MR, I walked out into the
horde of soldiers still standing, one of which had an /oDeath. Glad I
didn't try to kill them first.

I wished for:
Staff of Aesculcuslucsc
Orb of Fate
cloak of MR
gauntlets of power
boots of speed
helm of brilliance
shield of reflection

Well what do you know, the Staff of A is two-handed :(. A wish from
the throne got me an amulet of reflection. Did the quest (the monk
quest is supposed to be hard ?) and Ludios (too lazy to haul the gold
back up to minetown for protection, but I got disintegration res). I
discovered that the Staff of A is a  pretty awesome weapon.

Got the Eyes of the Overworld, blessed most of my armor to +5/+4 and
the Staff to +7, and blazed through Gehennom in just an hour or two.
The Eyes are lovely for this, plus blinding resistance was pretty
neat. VOTD left only one wraith corpse, which put me at XL16 (I'd
gotten to 15 through fighting at some point).

I intentionally fought every demon lord on the way down, for the hell
of it (pun not intended). I was hoping one of them would summon the
big D - Baalzebub summoned Geryon, but no go on any other demons. Oh
well. I'll make sure to let them all last longer next time I reach
Gehennom.

Vlad was a pushover, finding the VS was only mildly challenging, and
overall clearing everything up to waking Rodney was pretty simple.
Same as past experiences. So I stormed Rodney's tower (genocided c
during this, for some reason). Killing him once was no problem. Just
like before. No more Rodneys on the way down to the bottom of hell,
just one bolt of cursing or something.

Performed the invocation (with no trouble - last time I'd gotten this
far the bell had no charges and I had no way to charge it. Then,
rodney cursed the candelabrum and I had to climb out of hell to fix it
for the second time). The graveyard was no trouble, but no wraith
corpses. Rodney didn't show up until I had the outer chamber cleared
of priests and was searching for the entrance to the temple. When I
found it, I finished off the high priest with a single /oDeath hit
("You murderer!" gave me a laugh) and made for the stairs to kill
Rodney + clone.

I ended up stunned, which led to the discovery that both of my
unihorns were cursed. Damn. On the former VS floor I teleported to the
stairs and finished off Rodney, named the amulet !*REAL*! and made a
run for it. Rodney got an /oDigging and made me chase him and the
amulet back down ~8 floors.

 A few uneventful fights and several annoying throwbacks later, I'm
the in the VOTD (Rodney drops Snickersnee here). I climb out of hell
and run run run up to my closet altar, on DL8. Uncurse my spare
unihorn and bless the other (only 3 !owater) and I run up to DL1. I
make my last check for things I need in the planes. Finding nothing
missing, I enter the 'final test'.

(used forgotten spell + ?oGoldDetection for each one)

Plane of Earth is was easy enough. Minotaurs scared me, but the
Elvenking killed itself with lightning and Rodney was
uncharacteristically cooperative.

Plane of Air was scary. If lightning was straight lightning damage,
It'd be much less interesting. Got through eventually.

Plane of Fire gave me a fright, because I forgot I was confused and
stunned from the forgotten spell, and I walked into some lava. Oh
yeah, I still had my =olevitation on! Phew.

Plane of Water was boring with no ;. Rodney showed up no less than 3
times (one of my WoY meat tins is from here) . I eventually found the
magic portal under a gem or something.

The Astral Plane is funny, because you basically get a break.
Question: if your guardian angel dies (trapper ate it), and you put on
an =oconflict, do you still get the hostile angels?

Anyway, Pestilence left, Famine center, Death right. Went to the
center first, beat up a bunch of priests and angels, and found out the
altar was chaotic. Damn. Famine was laughably ineffective.

Went left, and found several artifacts near Pesty. Fire or Frostbrand,
maybe both, Demonbane, and Giantslayer (in the hands of 'Maud the
Swashbuckler'. Was hard to hit, must have had some nice AC). Anyway,
this altar was Lawful. I have to go rumble with Death. Oh well, the
other riders were pretty useless, right?

Man, Death is frightening. I started panicing when I realized he
drained max HP as well. I forgot about the *3* blessed !oFH I had,
too, even after Death downed one. He sucked about 50HP off my max, and
not being able to level drain made things tough, but he fell
eventually (after killing me once) and I got the hell past him. I just
pummeled past the priests and angels, knowing another fight with Death
would be my end. I got to the altar, #offered the Amulet, and turned
right around and smote Death where he stood (only a few spaces behind
me).

